  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDS Smart Metering Expansion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of a sovereign guaranteed loan in the amount of up to EUR 40 million  to Elektrodistribucija Srbije d.o.o. (&quot;EDS&quot;). The loan will finance first phase  of smart metering infrastructure in Serbian distribution system. A second phase  of the smart metering rollout is intended to be financed with EUR 40 million  from the EIB.  This project will support the introduction of Advanced Metering Infrastructure  (&quot;AMI&quot;), including modern meters together with related infrastructure,  software, communications equipment, installation and integration systems. The  roll-out of smart metering in Serbia will make a significant contribution to a  wider grid modernisation programme aimed at the development of a smart grid and  the reduction of technical and commercial losses, as well as the better  integration of distributed renewable generation sources in the system.  Furthermore, the enhanced functionality of smart meters will improve  demand-side management and lead to more efficient energy consumption.</narrative>
  </description>
